AWS Cloud — Advanced Real-World Scenarios Interview Questions
#AWS #DevOps #SRE 

Let’s take your AWS thinking to the next level!
 These questions reflect real-world reliability, automation, and scalability challenges faced by SREs and DevOps Engineers.

 Think about how you would solve them — not just which service to use. 💭👇

Your application running on EKS frequently restarts due to “OOMKilled” errors — how would you identify and resolve the issue?
Your production ALB starts returning intermittent 504 errors — what steps would you take to troubleshoot?
After deploying a new version via CodeDeploy, users report downtime — how can you achieve zero-downtime deployment next time?
One region has gone down — how do you design your system for high availability and disaster recovery across regions?
You suspect your S3 bucket has been accessed by an unauthorized user — how will you identify and secure it?
Your organization’s Lambda functions start exceeding concurrency limits — how will you mitigate this?
The EC2 instances behind your ASG are scaling up but the application remains slow — what could be the issue?
Your RDS database shows high read latency — how will you optimize it using AWS features?
CloudWatch shows CPU utilization at 100%, but the app’s performance is normal — what could explain this?
A CloudFormation stack deployment fails — how do you debug and safely roll back changes?
Your VPC network is experiencing high latency — how will you diagnose the bottleneck?
Your ECS tasks are failing during image pull — what could be the possible causes and fixes?
You need to automatically patch EC2 instances every weekend — how would you automate this process?
The DynamoDB table costs have increased drastically — how do you analyze and optimize the costs?
You want to enforce encryption on all S3 buckets across accounts — how can you achieve it at scale?
Developers need temporary AWS credentials for testing — how will you provide them securely?
You have multiple accounts and want to centralize logging — which AWS services and architecture will you use?
An API Gateway endpoint shows high latency — how do you troubleshoot performance from end to end?
Your CI/CD pipeline in CodePipeline fails during the “Build” phase — how do you investigate and fix it?
A CloudFront distribution isn’t updating content even after deployment — what could be wrong and how to fix it?

💡 Pro Tip:
 In real-world AWS environments, diagnostic thinking and root-cause analysis are just as important as knowing the right services.
